description:
**OUR TEAM** 




 You will join our eCommerce team, which is responsible for designing, developing, and maintaining some of the most innovative and market\-leading eCommerce applications and websites. Our team is dedicated to delivering world\-class user experiences, design excellence, and cutting\-edge web and mobile solutions that create an exciting and memorable journey for our customers.










**IDEAL CANDIDATE** 




 We are seeking a passionate and results\-driven Software Engineer (PHP/ Golang/ System) with strong hands\-on expertise in building and solving complex solutions. In this role, you will help lead the team in delivering scalable, maintainable, and innovative systems within a dynamic and fast\-paced environment.










**RESPONSIBILITIES** 



* Build highly scalable, reliable, and maintainable APIs to handle high\-volume transactions;
* We aim for teams that are inclusive, helpful, and have a strong sense of ownership for the things they build;
* Work closely with cross\-functional teams to define, design, and deliver new features;
* Work on addressing bugs and improving application performance;
* Continuously research, evaluate, and implement innovative technologies to optimize development efficiency and Customer Experience;
* Participate in the planning process for software development projects, ensuring adherence to quality standards and timely delivery;
* Design the architecture for new products and features;









**REQUIREMENTS** 




**Technical Skills:** 



* A pragmatic mindset;
* **3\+ years of experience** 
 with full lifecycle of project development for Golang Applications;
* Extensive experience in software design, architecture, development integration;
* Solid knowledge of event processing models, parallel programming, multi\-threading, enterprise integration pattern, Socket, Web Service, and REST;
* Distributed Caching such as Redis;
* Familiar with Microservices, event\-driven architecture;
* Good cross\-team communication skills;



**Soft skills:** 



* Excellent communication and teamwork abilities;
* Excellent problem\-solving and analytical skills;
* Strong willingness to learn new practices and technologies;
* Exceptional interpersonal skills, including facilitation and negotiation;
* Understanding and experience of Agile methodology;
* Experience in working across several technical domains with the ability to ‘deep dive’ where required and ensure correct solutions are implemented;









**BENEFITS** 



* Salary range: Open to negotiate;
* 13th\-month salary, annual salary review;
* Insurance will be paid according to company policy;
* Working devices provided, parking fee allowance (if any);
* Professional, dynamic, and friendly working environment and culture;








**WORKING PLACE:** 
 568 Luy Ban Bich St., Tan Phu Ward, Ho Chi Minh City










 If you need any further information, shoot me your CV at
 **thuyntt9@hasaki.vn** 
 to apply.










***\*\*\*Please note that only shortlisted candidates will be contacted. Thanks for your concern. ^^***

